[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-023-self-service-developer-portal-pattern.md#variation-2-custom-portal-with-multi-gateway-federation]

#### Variation 2: Custom Portal with Multi-Gateway Federation

**Use Case**: Enterprises with heterogeneous API gateway landscape (Azure APIM, Kong, AWS API Gateway) requiring unified developer experience across all platforms.

**Architecture:**
```text
Custom Developer Portal (React + Node.js)
    ├─ Gateway Abstraction Layer
    │   ├─ Azure APIM Adapter (REST API integration)
    │   ├─ Kong Gateway Adapter (Admin API integration)
    │   └─ AWS API Gateway Adapter (SDK integration)
    ├─ Unified API Catalog (aggregates from all gateways)
    ├─ Custom Documentation Generator (OpenAPI 3.0)
    ├─ Self-built Subscription Management
    ├─ Custom Analytics Dashboard (aggregates gateway logs)
    └─ Azure AD B2C or Auth0 (authentication)
```

**Implementation Example:**
```javascript
// Gateway Abstraction Layer - Adapter Pattern

// Base Gateway Interface
class GatewayAdapter {
  async listAPIs() { throw new Error('Not implemented'); }
  async getAPISpec(apiId) { throw new Error('Not implemented'); }
  async createSubscription(apiId, developerId) { throw new Error('Not implemented'); }
  async getUsageMetrics(subscriptionId, dateRange) { throw new Error('Not implemented'); }
}

// Azure APIM Adapter
class AzureAPIMAdapter extends GatewayAdapter {
  constructor(subscriptionId, resourceGroup, serviceName) {
    super();
    this.client = new ApiManagementClient(credentials, subscriptionId);
    this.resourceGroup = resourceGroup;
    this.serviceName = serviceName;
  }

  async listAPIs() {
    const apis = await this.client.api.listByService(
      this.resourceGroup,
      this.serviceName
    );
    return apis.map(api => ({
      id: api.name,
      name: api.displayName,
      version: api.apiVersion,
      description: api.description,
      gateway: 'azure-apim'
    }));
  }

  async getAPISpec(apiId) {
    const spec = await this.client.apiExport.get(
      this.resourceGroup,
      this.serviceName,
      apiId,
      'openapi-link'
    );
    return spec.value; // OpenAPI 3.0 specification
  }

  async createSubscription(apiId, developerId) {
    const subscription = await this.client.subscription.createOrUpdate(
      this.resourceGroup,
      this.serviceName,
      `sub-${developerId}-${apiId}`,
      {
        scope: `/apis/${apiId}`,
        displayName: `${developerId} subscription to ${apiId}`,
        state: 'active'
      }
    );
    return {
      subscriptionId: subscription.name,
      primaryKey: subscription.primaryKey,
      secondaryKey: subscription.secondaryKey
    };
  }
}

// Kong Gateway Adapter
class KongAdapter extends GatewayAdapter {
  constructor(adminApiUrl, apiKey) {
    super();
    this.adminUrl = adminApiUrl;
    this.headers = { 'Kong-Admin-Token': apiKey };
  }

  async listAPIs() {
    const response = await fetch(`${this.adminUrl}/services`, {
      headers: this.headers
    });
    const services = await response.json();
    return services.data.map(svc => ({
      id: svc.id,
      name: svc.name,
      version: svc.tags?.find(t => t.startsWith('version:'))?.split(':')[1],
      description: svc.tags?.join(', '),
      gateway: 'kong'
    }));
  }

  async createSubscription(apiId, developerId) {
    // Create Kong consumer
    const consumer = await fetch(`${this.adminUrl}/consumers`, {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { ...this.headers, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        username: developerId,
        custom_id: developerId
      })
    });

    // Create API key for consumer
    const keyResponse = await fetch(
      `${this.adminUrl}/consumers/${developerId}/key-auth`,
      {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { ...this.headers, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
      }
    );
    const keyData = await keyResponse.json();

    return {
      subscriptionId: keyData.id,
      primaryKey: keyData.key
    };
  }
}

// Unified Portal Service
class APIPortalService {
  constructor(gateways) {
    this.gateways = gateways; // Array of gateway adapters
  }

  async getAllAPIs() {
    // Aggregate APIs from all gateways
    const apiPromises = this.gateways.map(gw => gw.listAPIs());
    const apiArrays = await Promise.all(apiPromises);
    return apiArrays.flat();
  }

  async subscribeToAPI(apiId, developerId) {
    // Find which gateway owns this API
    const apis = await this.getAllAPIs();
    const api = apis.find(a => a.id === apiId);
    const gateway = this.gateways.find(gw => gw.constructor.name.includes(api.gateway));

    // Create subscription via appropriate gateway
    return await gateway.createSubscription(apiId, developerId);
  }
}

// Usage in Portal
const portalService = new APIPortalService([
  new AzureAPIMAdapter('sub-123', 'rg-prod', 'apim-gainwell'),
  new KongAdapter('https://kong-admin.internal:8001', 'admin-token')
]);

// Developer requests API list
const apis = await portalService.getAllAPIs();
// Returns unified list from both Azure APIM and Kong
```

**Pros:**
- ✅ Supports heterogeneous gateway environments
- ✅ Unified developer experience across all APIs
- ✅ Customizable to exact business requirements
- ✅ Full control over features and roadmap
- ✅ Can integrate third-party community platforms

**Cons:**
- ❌ Significant development and maintenance effort
- ❌ Requires expertise in all gateway platforms
- ❌ Synchronization complexity across gateways
- ❌ Higher total cost of ownership

